 *
 * E1M-EVK J7 -- the microSD slot, as the Zephyr disk "SD":
 *
 *   west build -b alp_e1m_aen803_m55_he/ae822fa0e5597ls0/rtss_he <app> -- \
 *     -DSHIELD=e1m_evk_microsd
 *
 * then disk_access_init("SD") or fs_mount() a FatFs volume on "/SD:".
 *
 * Carrier wiring (E1M-EVK-2626-R2):
 *   - The card sits behind the SDIO mux U38/U39. Its select input (E1M IO21)
 *     is not routed to firmware: header P18 open straps it LOW, which picks
 *     the microSD slot (P18 fitted picks the M.2 E-key card instead).
 *   - The mux output enable /E is E1M IO20, active low. On the E1M-AEN SoMs
 *     IO20 is a CC3501E GPIO, so it can only be driven once the CC3501E
 *     bridge is up: the app drives alp_gpio IO20 LOW before it first touches
 *     the disk. The SD host driver itself never touches the card before
 *     disk_access_init()/fs_mount(), so SD traffic starts only after the mux
 *     is enabled.
 *   - Use this shield only on a carrier whose U38/U39 are the reworked
 *     74LV3257 bus switches. The stock 74LVC157 parts always drive their
 *     outputs and fight the SoC's SD pins on EITHER /E state (see
 *     include/alp/boards/alp_e1m_evk.h), so leaving the mux disabled is not
 *     a safe fallback.
 *   - 4-bit, 3.3 V signalling only (no 1.8 V switch on the carrier), 25 MHz
 *     default speed.
 *
 * The SoC host node and its pins differ per SoM, so each supported target
 * has its own boards/<qualified-board>.overlay; the E1M-AEN targets share
 * boards/e1m_aen.dtsi.
 *
 * ADR 0017 Tier-1 (DT wiring only, no code).
 */
